 "notes_sources": {
  "title": "Notes, caveats and sources",
  "notes": [
   "How to read: 'Not found' means no reliable source was located. These cells were left empty rather than estimated.",
   "Height: elevations are published ranges (glacier or adjacent peak). No source gives a current (2026) measured height; surging glaciers can change by tens of metres in one event.",
   "Area: areas come from the 1973–2009 glacier inventory (S3); present-day areas will differ. Where sources conflict (e.g. Passu length 20.5–38 km) the range is shown.",
   "Distance: only distances reported by a source are shown, except Khurdopin–Shimshal, which is a straight-line formula from coordinates (not a flow-path distance).",
   "Population: sources differ by year and method; use the 2017 census or the district office for official figures.",
   "Confidence: High = several consistent sources; Medium = one good source or small conflicts; Low = limited or weak sources.",
   "Hispar, Barpu, Yazghil and Vijerab are in the Hunza basin but not directly beside the KKH; their settlement and population data were not researched."
  ],
